% Goods of chapters that the model does not have, from rulings of U.S.
% Customs and Border Protection (CROSS, rulings.cbp.gov), run through the
% whole modelled tariff (tariff.le) with the claims that the outside
% background (background/outside.le) raises from their words.
%
% Each good is of plastics, so the model alone puts it in heading 3926
% ("other articles of plastics"). But Chapter 39 note 2 sends a part of an
% electrical apparatus to Section XVI, a lamp and furniture to Chapter 94,
% sunglasses to Chapter 90, a pen and a tripod to Chapter 96. The model
% does not have those chapters. The outside background reads the good's
% name and raises a claim to the other heading. While the office has not
% answered the claim, the model's code is conditional: the answer names the
% judgment that it needs ("the claim ... is rejected"). When the office
% accepts the claim, as CBP did in each ruling, the model gives no code: the
% good belongs to a chapter that the model does not have.
%
% One scenario per ruling, named after it; each fact quotes the passage of
% the ruling that states it ("confer"). The claim is a fact of the outside
% background ("according to outside background, because <rule>"). CBP's
% code is in the comment above each scenario, not in the facts.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the tariff or of the rulings it
% cites, it is not a binding classification ruling, and it is not legal or
% customs advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them for a real
% import, export or declaration; consult the official texts, the customs
% authority and a qualified professional. Its authors accept no liability for
% any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base outside cbp includes these resources:
    marketplace.

the knowledge base outside cbp includes:

% Where each cited ruling is published, and a copy of its text (sources/).
ruling NY J86705 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/J86705".
the text of ruling NY J86705 is at "sources/cbp/J86705.txt".
ruling NY 803818 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/803818".
the text of ruling NY 803818 is at "sources/cbp/803818.txt".
ruling NY N304395 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N304395".
the text of ruling NY N304395 is at "sources/cbp/N304395.txt".
ruling NY N317961 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N317961".
the text of ruling NY N317961 is at "sources/cbp/N317961.txt".
ruling NY 882350 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/882350".
the text of ruling NY 882350 is at "sources/cbp/882350.txt".
ruling NY I84085 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/I84085".
the text of ruling NY I84085 is at "sources/cbp/I84085.txt".

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

query readings is:
    which good is classified in which code by which reading.

% NY J86705 (July 2003): a switch housing of plastic, the top of a control
% box with five buttons. CBP: 8538.90 (parts of apparatus of heading 8537).
% Before CBP answered: the code of Chapter 39 rests on the claim.
scenario ny_j86705_request is, as stated in ruling NY J86705:
    the switch housing is a manufactured article,
        confer "the switch housing, identified as item F29864-02, is the top portion of a control box".
    the switch housing is made of plastics,
        confer "It is comprised of plastic and contains five buttons".
    the principal use of the switch housing is closing a control box,
        according to CBP, confer "is the top portion of a control box".
    the switch housing is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI,
        according to outside background, because "claim_by_name",
        confer "The tariff classification of a switch housing from Japan".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the switch housing is 3926.90"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that the switch housing belongs to machinery of section XVI is rejected"].

% The same good once CBP has answered: the claim is accepted, and the model
% gives no code and does not report the good as unplaced.
scenario ny_j86705 is, as stated in ruling NY J86705:
    the switch housing is a manufactured article,
        confer "the switch housing, identified as item F29864-02, is the top portion of a control box".
    the switch housing is made of plastics,
        confer "It is comprised of plastic and contains five buttons".
    the principal use of the switch housing is closing a control box,
        according to CBP, confer "is the top portion of a control box".
    the switch housing is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI,
        according to outside background, because "claim_by_name",
        confer "The tariff classification of a switch housing from Japan".
    the claim that the switch housing belongs to machinery of section XVI is accepted,
        according to CBP,
        confer "The applicable subheading for the switch housing, item F29864-02, will be 8538.90.6000".
    subheading expects answers [].
    unplaced expects answers [].

% NY 803818 (November 1994): halogen desk lamps with a base and a head of
% plastics. CBP: 9405.20 (electric table and desk lamps).
scenario ny_803818 is, as stated in ruling NY 803818:
    the desk lamp is a manufactured article,
        confer "consists of halogen desk lamps".
    the desk lamp is made of plastics,
        confer "possessing base and head portions of plastics".
    the principal use of the desk lamp is lighting a desk,
        according to CBP, confer "consists of halogen desk lamps".
    the desk lamp is claimed to belong to lighting fittings of heading 9405,
        according to outside background, because "claim_by_name",
        confer "The tariff classification of plastic desk lamps from Taiwan".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the desk lamp is 3926.90"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that the desk lamp belongs to lighting fittings of heading 9405 is rejected"].

% NY N304395 (June 2019): promotional ball point pens of plastic. CBP:
% 9608.10 (ball point pens).
scenario ny_n304395 is, as stated in ruling NY N304395:
    the promotional pen is a manufactured article,
        confer "is described as a white plastic pen with removable plastic cap with clip".
    the promotional pen is made of plastics,
        confer "is described as a white plastic pen with removable plastic cap with clip".
    the principal use of the promotional pen is writing,
        according to CBP, confer "containing black ink".
    the promotional pen is claimed to belong to pens of heading 9608,
        according to outside background, because "claim_by_name",
        confer "identified as promotional ball point pens".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the promotional pen is 3926.90"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that the promotional pen belongs to pens of heading 9608 is rejected"].

% NY N317961 (March 2021): a tabletop tripod of plastic that holds a
% smartphone. CBP: 9620.00 (tripods, of plastics).
scenario ny_n317961 is, as stated in ruling NY N317961:
    style 7258 is a manufactured article,
        confer "This merchandise is a tabletop tripod stand designed to hold a smartphone for podcasting purposes".
    style 7258 is made of plastics,
        confer "According to the information provided, it is made primarily of plastic".
    the principal use of style 7258 is holding a smartphone,
        according to CBP, confer "This merchandise is a tabletop tripod stand designed to hold a smartphone for podcasting purposes".
    style 7258 is claimed to belong to tripods of heading 9620,
        according to outside background, because "claim_by_name",
        confer "This merchandise is a tabletop tripod stand designed to hold a smartphone for podcasting purposes".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style 7258 is 3926.90"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that style 7258 belongs to tripods of heading 9620 is rejected"].

% NY 882350 (February 1993): children's sunglasses of plastic. CBP:
% 9004.10 (sunglasses).
scenario ny_882350 is, as stated in ruling NY 882350:
    the sunglasses is a manufactured article,
        confer "They are sized for children and are not imported in a case.".
    the sunglasses is made of plastics,
        confer "The sunglasses are made of plastic and have plastic lenses.".
    the principal use of the sunglasses is protecting the eyes,
        according to CBP, confer "spectacles, goggles and the like".
    the sunglasses is claimed to belong to instruments of chapter 90,
        according to outside background, because "claim_by_name",
        confer "The sunglasses are made of plastic and have plastic lenses.".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the sunglasses is 3926.90"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that the sunglasses belongs to instruments of chapter 90 is rejected"].

% NY I84085 (July 2002): tables of woven resin wicker on metal frames.
% CBP: 9403.70 (furniture of plastics, household). The model alone reads a
% household article of plastics of heading 3924.
scenario ny_i84085 is, as stated in ruling NY I84085:
    the wicker table is a manufactured article,
        confer "The applicable subheading for the tables will be 9403.70.8010".
    the wicker table is made of plastics,
        confer "furniture items made of woven resin wicker on metal frames".
    the principal use of the wicker table is household use,
        according to CBP, confer "furniture of plastics: other, household".
    the wicker table is claimed to belong to furniture of chapter 94,
        according to outside background, because "claim_by_name",
        confer "The applicable subheading for the tables will be 9403.70.8010".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the wicker table is 3924.90"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that the wicker table belongs to furniture of chapter 94 is rejected"].

% A listing of a phone case of plastics that holds a lithium battery ("Is
% Electric: Lithium Battery"), read with the background: the uses
% background gives the use of a phone case (HQ H284146), and the outside
% background raises a claim to Section XVI, because a case with a battery
% is a power bank of heading 8507 (NY N265396). The listing reading does
% not admit the uses background, so it gives no code; the two readings that
% do give a code conditional on the claim, because each reading admits the
% outside background.
scenario battery_case is, as stated in the listing:
    the battery case is classified under the US tariff.
    the battery case is a manufactured article, according to marketplace listings, because "finished_product", confer "Phone Case".
    the battery case is made of plastics, according to materials background, because "plastics_by_name", confer "Material: Plastic".
    the principal use of the battery case is other use, according to uses background, because "use_by_name", confer "Phone Case".
    the battery case is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI, according to outside background, because "claim_by_power_field", confer "Is Electric: Lithium Battery".
    readings expects answers [
        "the battery case is classified in 3926.90 by presumed reading",
        "the battery case is classified in 3926.90 by usage reading"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that the battery case belongs to machinery of section XVI is rejected"].
